WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.189 --> 00:00:07.410
If the plethora of Marvel and DC films aren't
enough to soothe your superhero cravings,

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.250
you might want to see what other countries
have to offer.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:16.010
Sure, these movies might not be as technically
impressive as the superpowered blockbusters

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:21.630
we're used to—but they feature enough culture
shock quirks to warrant a watch.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:27.490
Let's take a trip across the globe and see
the strangest superhero films released outside

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.490
the United States.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:31.380
Guardians - Russia

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:36.540
If you thought Guardians of the Galaxy needed
less humor and more super ripped bears, you'll

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.550
be thrilled with 2017's Guardians.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:44.920
This Russian superhero epic looks like a knockoff
Marvel film with about a quarter of the budget.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.739
There's acrobatic fighting, insane weapons,
and gorgeous people doing battle — all the

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:51.269
modern superhero hallmarks.

00:00:51.269 --> 00:00:55.820
But Russia really brings the weird with Ursus
the werebear.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:00.499
Unlike werewolves, Ursus doesn't have to wait
for a full moon to take bear form — he can

00:01:00.499 --> 00:01:02.139
do it whenever he wants.

00:01:02.139 --> 00:01:07.230
Or if he'd rather just be half-man, half-bear,
that's an option too — which leads to the

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:12.150
best moment of the trailer: seeing a man-bear
fire off a machine gun.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.100
The Heroic Trio - China

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.750
When it comes to female superheroes, China
has us beat.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:24.320
1992's The Heroic Trio is about a squad of
three superpowered women united to stop a

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:29.310
supernatural villain whose main goal is to
find a king for China.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:35.270
He's kidnapped 18 male babies, and one will
become the ruler of the land; the others will

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:37.910
be groomed to form an army of killers.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.400
The plot may sound a little bit odd, but if
you want to see flying motorcycles cut in

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:50.910
half, or a leather-clad lady riding a dynamite-fueled
barrel, your only choice is The Heroic Trio.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.580
Three Supermen and Mad Girl - Turkey

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.920
Why settle for one Superman when you can have
three?

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:03.060
Turkey has made a lot of knockoff superhero
movies, but perhaps the strangest is 1973's

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.460
Three Supermen and Mad Girl.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:11.910
Three low-rent Superman knock-offs fight off
an evil foe named Mad Girl ... for some reason.

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:18.200
There's also an old fashioned, definitely-made-from-a-cardboard-box
robot who plagues our heroes with his death

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.200
ray.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.720
Will our Supermen prevail?

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.340
Is that actually supposed to be the devil,
or just a guy in a mask?

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:27.730
Watch all 65 minutes to find out!

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.610
Zebraman - Japan

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:36.110
If you combined Breaking Bad with Kick-Ass,
you'd get 2004's Japanese action comedy Zebraman.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:41.630
It's about a failed teacher and family man
who escapes from his depressing life by secretly

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:48.800
dressing up like an unpopular 1970s TV superhero
called — you guessed it — Zebraman.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:55.030
But unlike Kick-Ass, the protagonist of Zebraman
soon learns he actually does have superpowers,

00:02:55.030 --> 00:03:00.500
so he uses them to defeat alien-possessed
baddies set on conquering Earth.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.910
RA.One - India

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:08.140
It looks a lot like some kind of Indian Iron
Man, but 2010's RA.One is not a blatant Marvel

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.140
copy.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.160
It's more like a Tron/Iron Man mashup.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:16.200
A programmer creates a video game with a very
powerful villain named RA.One.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.530
Unfortunately, the villain escapes the game
and enters the real world, so the game's creator

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:26.140
must transform into a hero named G. One to
defeat him.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.709
Chakra the Invincible - India

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:33.470
Did you know Marvel legend Stan Lee also created
an Indian superhero?

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:38.960
Chakra the Invincible is Lee's first venture
outside the U.S., and so far, the hero has

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:44.100
an animated film for Cartoon Network India
and a live-action version in development.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:50.090
The story is about Raju Rai, a young kid who
tries on a blue bodysuit that gives him spiritually-derived

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:55.640
superpowers that turn him into Chakra the
Invincible, protector of Mumbai.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.780
The Return of Captain Invincible - Australia

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:05.210
The plot of 1983's Australian superhero parody
The Return of Captain Invincible is unusual,

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:06.580
to say the least.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:12.510
Alan Arkin's Captain Invincible is America's
go-to superhero during World War II, but during

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:17.540
the McCarthy trials, he's ruled a danger to
the country and no longer allowed to fight

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.540
crime.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:22.870
Cut to the '80s, when a villain played by
Christopher Lee gets control of a hypno-ray

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:26.320
that causes people to laugh uncontrollably.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:32.590
The U.S. must find Captain Invincible, who's
now a terrible drunk hiding out in Australia.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.000
Also, it's a musical …

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.450
"Where angels fear to tread / I say, 'Choose
your booze!

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:40.690
Let's hit the red eye!'"

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:42.830
Mr. and Mrs. Incredible - Hong Kong

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:48.880
2011's Hong Kong action comedy Mr. and Mrs.
Incredible is about a retired husband-and-wife

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:52.780
crime fighting duo who have to deal with the
issues of a normal life.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:59.150
Are they inspired by The Incredibles, Pixar's
2004 film about a retired superhero family?

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.300
Probably!

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:05.770
But the folks at Pixar haven't sued anybody
over it yet — maybe they're fans?

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:09.940
Unlike the family favorite, the Hong Kong
version partly revolves around the husband

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:14.690
losing interest in sex with his wife until
a new hot lady comes to town.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:19.970
But husband Gazer Warrior, who shoots lightning
from his eyes, and wife Aroma Woman, who puts

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:26.490
men into a trance with her alluring odor,
end up rekindling the spark in their marriage—all

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.450
while wrangling their giant goldfish.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:31.199
Rendel - Finland

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:36.220
Perhaps the most conventional film on this
list, Finland's Rendel is about Punisher-like

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:40.930
figure looking to take down a criminal organization
that murdered his family.

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:45.540
Not much is known about the Nordic nation's
first masked vigilante, but the trailer for

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:52.560
the Indiegogo-financed flick, due out in the
Fall of 2017, hints at a dark, slick dystopian

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:56.310
tale with production values that belie its
humble origins.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:06:01.980
We do know for certain it's the only superhero
movie with official promotional condoms.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:04.680
Your move, Deadpool 2.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:05.680
Thanks for watching!

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.520
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:11.270
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

